#: site/index.njk:1
msgid ""
"Meet Habibi, an open-source personal AI companion in development. Local "
"memory, your choice of AI provider, and encrypted sync designed to keep you "
"in control."
msgstr ""

#: site/index.njk:69
msgid ""
"Memory, search, and the agent loop stay local. Your devices hold the vault "
"key and encrypt content before sync."
msgstr ""

#: site/_includes/layout.njk:59
msgid "No analytics. No trackers. Just a hello."
msgstr ""

#: site/index.njk:85
msgid "No fine print."
msgstr ""

#: site/index.njk:61
msgid ""
"No mystery about what’s being built. The code, decisions, and rough edges "
"belong in the open, so you can look inside, ask questions, or make it your "
"own."
msgstr ""

#: site/index.njk:91
msgid ""
"No. Local-first describes where memory, search, and the agent loop are "
"intended to live. Using a remote inference provider requires a connection "
"and sends selected context to that provider. There’s no planned silent "
"fallback to a different remote provider."
msgstr ""

#: site/index.njk:75
msgid ""
"Not a promise of invisibility. A clear boundary around who can read what."
msgstr ""

#: site/index.njk:54
msgid "Not a user profile."
msgstr ""

#: site/index.njk:80
msgid "Not quite in your pocket."
msgstr ""

#: site/index.njk:90
msgid ""
"Not yet. This is an early open-source project, starting with a ciphertext-"
"only sync prototype, not a released mobile app. The interface above is a "
"concept. There’s no launch date or waitlist; you can follow progress and "
"explore the code on"
