#: site/index.njk:88
msgid ""
"The design keeps synced content encrypted with a random vault key owned by "
"your devices. The service stores ciphertext, not readable memories, content "
"keys, or inference-provider credentials. It still sees account and "
"operational sync metadata, such as object sizes and when sync requests "
"happen. This is not anonymity."
msgstr ""

#: site/index.njk:80
msgid ""
"The plan is deliberately small: an Elixir backend, Postgres for a little "
"metadata, and affordable S3-compatible storage for encrypted objects. "
"Stateless sync servers that can grow without becoming a home for your "
"readable memories."
msgstr ""

#: site/index.njk:71
msgid ""
